          "text": "A CDN serves stale content only when revalidation or failure fallback is explicitly permitted"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Fresh responses are served directly; once stale, the CDN should revalidate or fetch a new representation unless stale-while-revalidate or stale-if-error applies.",
          "bullet": false
        },
        {
          "text": "Without an applicable stale rule, inspect Age, Warning, response headers, and provider behavior rather than assuming stale delivery is valid.",
          "bullet": false
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Decision path: serve a fresh hit; serve stale during permitted background revalidation; serve stale on permitted upstream failure; otherwise revalidate or fetch. Use Age, Warning, response headers, and observed CDN behavior to diagnose exceptions."
}

